 "text": "Starting a new goal feels better than finishing the old one. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 28. Week one of guitar you're buzzing. Week six it's hard chords and sore fingers. Then a Spanish video shows up and the buzz is back. A new goal starts at zero where every step feels huge and planning it feels like progress. So the guitar never gets finished, it gets replaced. The fix before adding a goal give the old one its next finish line. Guitar one full song by month end. The new goal goes on a later list with a date, Spanish, December 1st. It's parked and the guitar gets its four weeks. Send this to the friend with five half-started goals. That's what D-Mure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, next, why you can't see yourself getting better. Which goal did you start then replace, the links in the bio.",
